// hex_shape — the shape vocabulary — the line primitive, the box, the arc.
//
// The rest of `𝕄*` beside the turtle form: a WALL as a line primitive with a constant width
// (never a count of lattice rows), the BOX in 12 directions with its two orbits, and the ARC
// whose centre is exact and whose radius quantises to a realisable shell.
//
// Entry point: re-exports `hexwall`, `hexbox`, `hexarc`.
use hexwall;
use hexbox;
use hexarc;
